{
  "$schema": "../scene.schema.json",
  "id": "moorings-watch",
  "name": "Mooring's Watch",
  "description": "Bead mw-e25.6 (with the forest-loop leg of mw-e25.25): the abandoned barony watchtower, a 180 x 100 m greybox on its spur. From the west gap (spur-gate, back to the Briarwood's moorings-gate; arrive-from-briarwood) the spur trail runs east between drop-off walls to the goblin lookout camp below the curtain wall (goblin-lookout, a ladder post at lookout-post), then through the courtyard gate (courtyard-gate) into the courtyard (moorings-courtyard). The tower (moorings-tower; region tower, which doubles as the Hollow Sentinels' leash volume) takes four floors of 3 m: the armour stand hall (armour-stand-a to d), the keeper's quarters with the keepers-log desk, the bell cord shaft (bell-cord, hanging through the roof) and the roof (tower-roof) with the signal-mirror plinth. Stairs wind up inside (three flights); two climbs go up outside, ivy on the south face (everyone: walk into it) and broken masonry on the east face (rough: a jump at it, thief and archer only). The supply tunnel's cellar door (supply-tunnel-door, lock tunnel-collapsed) stands in the courtyard's north wall, shut over a sealed vestibule: the tunnel beyond is mw-e26 and the way through it is mw-e25.9. A second gap in the north wall (ridge-gate, arrive-from-briarwood-ridge) is the start of the ridge path to the Briarwood's priory road. East of the courtyard a plain of crags stands in for the valley (view it from roof-view). Encounters (mw-e25.7) and the signal mirror puzzle (mw-e25.8) are not built.",
  "grid": 1,
